# Hand-authored keystone regressions. One JSON object per line (JSONL).
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Schema: the canonical `Fixture<E2ETransition>` (holon-pbt-core) serde shape —
#   {"name": <slug>, "description": <provenance>, "transitions": [<E2ETransition>, ...]}
# The Fixture-only `environment`/`initial_state` fields are omitted here (serde-default):
# the base state is the fixed `wide_e2e_ref()`, not a serialized ReferenceState.
# Each transition is the production `E2ETransition` enum in serde's external-tag form:
#   {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "...", "id": "block:..."}}
#   {"BlockToPage": {"origin_id": "block:..."}}
# Replayed over `wide_e2e_ref()` (full_headless wiring) by tests/hand_authored_regressions.rs.
#
# --- liveness smoke: a clean create must stay GREEN -----------------------------------------
# Proves the harness is not rigged to always panic: a bread-and-butter create the random
# keystone runs constantly. Runs first; must pass before the red case below is reached.
{"name": "create-block-smoke", "description": "harness liveness: a lone clean create under the focused page passes the full invariant catalog", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "clean smoke", "id": "block:smoke0"}}]}
#
# --- editor same-seq trailing-whitespace echo (EditorBufferOwnership Inc 4) -----------------
# Repro of the SqlOnly editor "typed trailing space vanishes ~100ms later" P1. Create a block
# "foo", open its editor, type ONE trailing space. The cell-free editor VM stamps write_seq on
# `set_field("foo ")`; the SQL provider trims trailing whitespace on store and echoes "foo" back
# carrying the SAME write_seq. `evaluate_data_sync_echo` MUST recognise this as the editor's own
# canonicalization (`AdoptBaseline`) and KEEP the typed "foo " buffer, not Converge to "foo".
# GREEN with the guard's trim-shape discriminator present; RED (buffer regresses to "foo",
# `inv-editor-text/mirror` mismatch on block:echo0) on a throwaway revert of that discriminator.
{"name": "editor-trailing-space-echo-adopts-baseline", "description": "Inc4 echo lock: same-seq trailing-ws echo must keep the typed buffer (AdoptBaseline), not regress it (Converge)", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "foo", "id": "block:echo0"}}, {"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:echo0"}}, {"TypeChars": {"text": " "}}]}

# --- block-to-page on '/'-containing content (dogfood 2026-07-20, bug a1) -------------------
# Repro: create a block whose content contains a trailing '/', then convert it to a page.
# The planner (PageId::for_path) splits the origin content on '/', so a trailing '/' yields an
# empty path segment and fails loud ("... has an empty segment ..."). The keystone's reference
# oracle mirrors that same content-as-path assumption, so this case goes RED on the unfixed base.
# Becomes the permanent regression lock: green once content is treated as a single leaf page name.
# RETIRED 2026-07-22 (row-28 lane): the '/'-content target of this case is FIXED. The backend
# sanitize (land 866977e85e) strips a trailing '/' from the page title; the keystone oracle now
# MIRRORS it (transitions/block_to_page.rs::sanitize_page_leaf, used by plan_new_page for the page
# id and by reference_state::apply_block_to_page for the page content), so a BlockToPage on
# trailing-'/' content reconciles born-equal on both sides (proved: the page block is "Slashy block"
# on both, and the harness.rs:603 synthetic/real id-reconcile now balances). This case can NO LONGER
# run to green here for an UNRELATED reason: replayed standalone (not generated), it also surfaces a
# hand-authored-replay-only org/loro divergence on the boot-fired journal day-page ("2026-01-15" under
# block:journals) + a __document_root__ sentinel that the SUT org snapshot does not read in the direct
# test_sequential path (the GENERATED keystone reads it fine — inv-blocks-match-ref/org is green there).
# That residual is a hand-authored-replay harness gap, NOT the '/'-content bug, and is tracked in
# docs/Testing/BugFunnel.md. Re-enable once the replay path materialises/reads the boot-journal file.
# {"name": "block-to-page-slash-content-empty-segment", "description": "dogfood 2026-07-20 bug (a1): convert_block_to_page planner treats origin content as a /-split page path; trailing/embedded '/' -> empty-segment fail-loud", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "Slashy block/", "id": "block:slashy"}}, {"BlockToPage": {"origin_id": "block:slashy"}}]}
#
# --- mark-bounds coverage note (dogfood 2026-07-20, journal-click SIGABRT) --------------------
# The mark-outlives-content corruption (a persisted link mark whose span exceeds its block
# content -> `scalar_range_to_bytes` aborts EVERY render) is NOT reachable via a hand-authored
# create+convert here: the SUT trims content on every write (`SqlOperationProvider::trimmed_content`),
# so `convert_block_to_page` derives its full-span link mark from ALREADY-TRIMMED content, and the
# harness applies plan+apply atomically (no shrink window). A trailing-space create instead trips
# the ref/SUT content-trim asymmetry (`inv-block-content/*`, `inv-displayed-text/*`) — a separate
# reference-model bug, not this one. The mark-bounds invariant (`inv-mark-bounds-within-content`)
# DOES engage on the slash convert case above (3/3) and on every backend-bearing slice; its teeth
# are proven by the unit catch test in
# `pbt::composed::invariants::mark_bounds_within_content::tests`. A keystone RED needs a
# fault-injection transition that writes a mark span decoupled from a shorter content (or a
# store-divergence create) — tracked as a coverage follow-up.


# --- external-write-while-focused: dirty-buffer preservation lock (EBO seam, vault row-292) ---
# Focus -> Type (dirty) -> ExternalWriteWhileFocused. The random generator almost never lands the
# dirty-editor window at a step where this transition is sampled, so a deterministic hand-authored
# case is the only way to exercise it. NOTE: hand-authored replay drives transitions directly and
# BYPASSES the HOLON_PBT_EXTERNAL_RACES generator gate (the gate is generator-only); preconditions
# (app_started + active_editor_dirty + has_document_uri) are the only admission checks, and the
# create/focus/type prefix establishes the dirty editor, so the case runs with the flag UNSET.
{"name": "external-write-while-focused-preserves-dirty-buffer", "description": "EBO seam / vault row-292: an external sibling-add re-ingest landing while a focused block has a DIRTY editor buffer must NOT clobber that buffer (inv-editor-text/mirror = no silent data loss) nor duplicate blocks (inv-live-children-match-ref). Prefix mirrors the green echo case: create wwf0 under the structural-page focus root, focus it, type DIRTY. Then an external write adds a sibling to the SAME doc mid-focus.", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "wwf-focus", "id": "block:wwf0"}}, {"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:wwf0"}}, {"TypeChars": {"text": "DIRTY"}}, {"ExternalWriteWhileFocused": {"doc_uri": "block:structural-page", "blocks": [{"id": "block:wwf-ext0", "parent_id": "block:structural-page", "content": "external sibling", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}]}}]}
#
# --- ref-doc-0 remap gap: born-equal create-under-focus (BugFunnel 2026-07-22, keystone tolerated red) ---
# Deterministic repro of the ref-doc-0 remap gap. CreateDocument mints the ORACLE's synthetic
# `block:ref-doc-0`; the SUT writes an empty doc_0.org whose watcher mints a REAL uuid, so the two
# id-spaces differ (per-tick reconcile maps ref-doc-0 -> uuid). NavigateFocus focuses the ORACLE's
# `block:ref-doc-0`. CreateBlockUnderFocus with an EXPLICIT id (`id: Some(...)`, born-equal path)
# dispatches `block.create{parent_id: <focus-root>}` DIRECTLY (components.rs create_block_with_id),
# and create_block_under_focus.rs passes the UNREMAPPED oracle focus-root `block:ref-doc-0` as the
# parent -> SUT Loro has no such block -> "parent block not found: block:ref-doc-0" hard failure.
# The `id: None` slot path dodges this (commit_creation_slot re-resolves the parent from the SUT's
# own live rows), which is why the earlier hand-authored case was green. GREEN once the SUT
# create-under-focus resolves the focus-root parent through the id resolver (remap TOTAL, fail-loud
# on an unmapped synthetic). NB: the BugFunnel row's phantom signature was WRONG — the live
# manifestation is this hard create failure, not an inv-viewmodel-entity-ids-subset-of-data phantom.
# NB: uses a SINGLE CreateDocument. A 2nd CreateDocument confounds this lock with a SEPARATE
# doc-ingest history under-recording (harness.rs:300 counts each ref-doc-N->uuid remap as a UI
# create that must record >=1 block_history op_group, but the 2nd doc's watcher-ingest records
# none) -> inv-history-records-all-creates fires BEFORE CreateBlockUnderFocus even runs, masking
# the parent-resolution bug. One doc keeps the born-equal create reachable. (2nd-doc issue parked.)
{"name": "ref-doc-0-remap-born-equal-create-under-focus", "description": "BugFunnel 2026-07-22 ref-doc-0 remap gap: born-equal (id:Some) CreateBlockUnderFocus under a CreateDocument-minted synthetic doc dispatches block.create with the UNREMAPPED oracle focus-root parent -> SUT parent-not-found. Green once the focus-root parent is resolved through the id resolver.", "transitions": [{"CreateDocument": {"file_name": "doc_0.org"}}, {"NavigateFocus": {"region": "main", "block_id": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "a", "id": "block:gen-13"}}]}
#
# --- ref-doc-0 remap gap FACET 2: undo over-reverts a file-ingested doc (BugFunnel 2026-07-22) ---
# The ORIGINAL BugFunnel phantom (inv-viewmodel-entity-ids-subset-of-data), an ORACLE-side undo bug.
# CreateBlockUnderFocus(g0) is a USER-origin block.create -> pushes an oracle undo snapshot S0 taken
# BEFORE g0 (so S0 has NO docs) and is undoable in prod. CreateDocument writes doc_0.org whose
# watcher-ingest mints the doc page: in the ORACLE `insert_document` adds it to the SNAPSHOTTED
# block_state.blocks (+ files.documents, which is NOT snapshotted); in the SUT it is an INGEST-origin
# create that (operation_engine.rs:1220 "only User-origin ops push undo entries") is NOT on the undo
# stack. UndoLastMutation pops S0 -> the ORACLE block_state loses the doc block, but PROD's
# engine.undo() only reverts g0 and KEEPS the file-ingested doc. So the SUT still renders the doc
# (sidebar page list) while the resolved oracle no longer knows it -> phantom entity id. Fix is
# ORACLE-side & prod-faithful: file-ingested doc pages (tracked in files.documents) must survive
# undo like next_doc_id already does (reference_state.rs:1863) -> re-materialise dropped doc roots
# after pop_undo_to_redo. GREEN once the oracle undo stops over-reverting file docs.
{"name": "ref-doc-0-undo-over-reverts-file-ingested-doc", "description": "BugFunnel 2026-07-22 ref-doc-0 FACET 2 (the original subset-of-data phantom): a USER-origin CreateBlockUnderFocus snapshots pre-doc state; a CreateDocument file-ingest (INGEST-origin, not undoable in prod) adds the doc; UndoLastMutation restores the pre-doc oracle snapshot, dropping the doc oracle-side while prod KEEPS it -> the SUT-rendered doc is a phantom against the resolved oracle. Oracle-side undo over-reverts file-ingested docs.", "transitions": [{"CreateBlockUnderFocus": {"content": "g", "id": "block:gen-0"}}, {"CreateDocument": {"file_name": "doc_0.org"}}, {"UndoLastMutation": null}]}
